{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01557",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.7,
      "end_seconds": 4.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Sorry, doctor, shall I sit here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.46,
      "end_seconds": 9.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.37,
      "end_seconds": 21.41,
      "duration_seconds": 11.04,
      "text": "Yeah, it's heavy bleeding after the birth. I don't know what's causing it. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.7,
      "end_seconds": 25.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.24,
      "end_seconds": 44.6,
      "duration_seconds": 18.36,
      "text": "For five days, I'd say. As for passing large clots, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. I've also been feeling faint."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.5,
      "end_seconds": 49.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "And what about fever, severe pain or headache?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.86,
      "end_seconds": 54.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "No, no fever, severe pain or headache."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.83,
      "end_seconds": 64.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Alright, what about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.06,
      "end_seconds": 67.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.85,
      "end_seconds": 72.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "So, how are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.82,
      "end_seconds": 78.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, no, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.58,
      "end_seconds": 82.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.61,
      "end_seconds": 95.99,
      "duration_seconds": 12.38,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.28,
      "end_seconds": 105.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.18,
      "end_seconds": 114.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "Clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day for the stent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.32,
      "end_seconds": 120.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.39,
      "end_seconds": 122.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "No known allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.03,
      "end_seconds": 126.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.91,
      "end_seconds": 129.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Yes, heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.37,
      "end_seconds": 139.44,
      "duration_seconds": 8.07,
      "text": "Okay, I can see heart disease in your file as well. Have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.49,
      "end_seconds": 145.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Just an operation for a hernia, last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.56,
      "end_seconds": 163.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.16,
      "end_seconds": 177.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.85,
      "end_seconds": 205.96,
      "duration_seconds": 13.11,
      "text": "Okay: oxygen saturation is 96 percent, pulse 106, temperature 37.1, weight 70 kilos, height 153 centimetres, pressure 94 over 65, respiratory rate 19, BMI works out to 29.9."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.86,
      "end_seconds": 212.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.49,
      "end_seconds": 232.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.81,
      "end_seconds": 235.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.62,
      "end_seconds": 250.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "You are pale and clammy and the womb feels soft and large."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.32,
      "end_seconds": 270.52,
      "duration_seconds": 14.2,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. Let me tell you where I've got to. I think we're dealing with a postpartum haemorrhage at this stage. It could also be retained tissue, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.53,
      "end_seconds": 275.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.14,
      "end_seconds": 301.27,
      "duration_seconds": 25.13,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a postpartum haemorrhage, and we'll know more once the an urgent scan is back. An urgent scan is what I'd like next, for bleeding. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. I'm going to order urgent blood tests, for haemorrhage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.62,
      "end_seconds": 305.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Do I need to prepare?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.98,
      "end_seconds": 325.59,
      "duration_seconds": 18.61,
      "text": "For this, oxytocin, 10 units, now, single dose. It's for postpartum bleeding. I am rubbing the womb to help it contract, and calling the emergency team. The obstetric team would be the right next step, I'll refer you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.17,
      "end_seconds": 326.87,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.08,
      "end_seconds": 343.41,
      "duration_seconds": 11.33,
      "text": "The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. What are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.45,
      "end_seconds": 351.55,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "So, I take the oxytocin, 10 units, now. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.04,
      "end_seconds": 359.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Right, does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.55,
      "end_seconds": 363.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.56,
      "end_seconds": 367.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}